# owl-intersection-of: a small runnable case for EYE RPO rules.
# Source: https://eyereasoner.github.io/eye/reasoning/rpo/owl-intersectionOf.n3
# Rules: MIT, Jos De Roo; sample data added for this example.
# The all-members test uses log:forAllIn in place of e:findall.

@prefix : <http://example.org/>.
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>.
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>.
@prefix list: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/list#>.
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#>.

# Sample data
:WorkingStudent owl:intersectionOf (:Student :Worker). :alice a :WorkingStudent. :bob a :Student, :Worker.

# Inference rules
@prefix list: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/list#>.
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>.
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>.
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>.
@prefix e: <http://eulersharp.sourceforge.net/2003/03swap/log-rules#>.

{?C owl:intersectionOf ?L. ?X a ?C. ?D list:in ?L} => {?X a ?D}.
{?C owl:intersectionOf ?L. ?D list:in ?L} => {?C rdfs:subClassOf ?D}.
{ ?C owl:intersectionOf ?L. ?L list:first ?First. ?X a ?First. ({?D list:in ?L} {?X a ?D}) log:forAllIn ?SCOPE } => {?X a ?C}.
